Regev {[}Reg05{]} defined the \emph{learning with error} (LWE) problem,
which can be phrased as a bounded-distance problem on Λ(\textbf{A})
where \textbf{A} is chosen uniformly at random. He showed that LWE is
hard on the average unless there is an efficient \emph{quantum}
algorithm for solving SIVP and GapSVP on \emph{any} lattice of dimension
\emph{n} to within˜\emph{O}(\emph{n}) factors.

We now state a few important facts about these random lattices that will
be used throughout the rest of the paper. The first is a lemma on
additive groups going back to {[}Ajt96{]}; the tightest version we know
of was proved in {[}Reg05{]}.
