\begin{quote}
\emph{pairs} (which can be based on the hardness of ISIS). The essential
idea is that repeated signature queries on the same message \emph{m}
will all have distinct salts \emph{r} (except with negligible
probability \emph{Q}2 sign\emph{/}2\emph{k}), so the signer will provide
a preimage for independent hash values \emph{H}(\emph{m∥r}).
\end{quote}

